<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#englishry">Glossary</a> · Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Englishry</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Englishry was the lowland part of a marcher lordship in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wales">Wales</a>, settled by English and Flemish colonists and run under English law and manorial custom, as distinct from the upland <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/welshry">Welshry</a>, where Welsh tenants kept Welsh law and customs. The division was clearest in lordships such as Gower and Pembroke, whose English-speaking south long remained distinct.</p></div>
